{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q005_cupredoxin_function_transfer","answer":"SCOPe 2.08 places all three in the Cupredoxins superfamily b.6.1 (SUNID 49503), within the Cupredoxin-like fold b.6 (49502) and All beta proteins class b (48724). They are distinct families: Plastocyanin/azurin-like b.6.1.1 (49504), Ephrin ectodomain b.6.1.5 (74874), and Peptidylarginine deiminase PAD4, N-terminal domain b.6.1.6 (110107). The fold is a Greek-key beta sandwich, typically seven strands in two sheets. Shared superfamily membership expresses probable common ancestry, stronger than sharing a fold or class alone, but does not imply identical function or close sequence similarity.

Copper binding and electron transfer must not be transferred across these families. Canonical plastocyanin and azurin are copper-dependent electron carriers, whereas SCOPe explicitly describes both ephrin ectodomains and the PAD4 N-terminal domain as probably related to cupredoxins but lacking the metal-binding site. Ephrins function in receptor-mediated signaling; PAD4 is a calcium-dependent peptidylarginine deiminase, and classification of its N-terminal domain does not assign that domain the catalytic activity of the whole enzyme. Neither should be annotated as a copper-binding electron carrier from superfamily membership.

A shared scaffold can guide structural comparison, but functional transfer requires target-specific conservation of coordinating residues and their geometry, evidence of copper occupancy or binding, and biochemical evidence of redox/electron-transfer activity. A structural template alone establishes none of these.","evidence_used":["Pretrained model knowledge","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__list_scop_children","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Cupredoxin&mode=auto&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49502","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49502/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49502/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49502/children?limit=30","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49503/children?limit=30","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49504","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/74874","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/74874/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110107","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/110107/annotations"]}]}
